title: Provinces
subtitle: The German states: their parliaments, their governments and the party's work in them.
is-pinned-card: true
tags: rf_top
new-page: true
on-arrival: {! window.RF.provincesView(Q); !}

= The States

The Reich is a federation of eighteen states, each with its own parliament, government and police. Choose a state to see its Landtag and the party's work there. The party can take one decision in the states each month.

[+ states_view +]

- @prussia
- @bavaria
- @saxony
- @wurttemberg
- @baden
- @thuringia
- @hesse
- @hamburg
- @mschwerin
- @oldenburg
- @brunswick
- @anhalt
- @bremen
- @lippe
- @lubeck
- @mstrelitz
- @waldeck
- @slippe
- @rf_hand: Back to the party.

@prussia
title: Prussia
new-page: true
on-arrival: {! window.RF.stateView(Q, 'prussia'); !}

= Prussia

[+ st_view +]

- @prussia_campaign
- @prussia_councils
- @prussia_support
- @prussia_attack
- @prussia_ruhr
- @rf_provinces: Back to the states.
- @rf_hand: Back to the party.

@prussia_campaign
title: Campaign in Prussia.
subtitle: Meetings, leaflets and the party press. Raises the party's standing here. Costs 1 resource.
new-page: true
choose-if: prov_ready = 1 and funds >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: One decision in the states a month; needs 1 resource.
on-arrival: {!
Q.funds -= 1;
Q.members += 1;
window.RF.stateAction(Q, 'prussia', 2.0);
!}

= Prussia

Speakers tour the industrial towns, the local party paper doubles its run for a week, and the comrades go door to door in the workers' districts.

- @prussia: Back to Prussia.
- @rf_hand: Back to the party.

@prussia_councils
title: Organise the factory councils and the unemployed in Prussia.
subtitle: More influence in the unions, a little more standing here. The police take note.
new-page: true
choose-if: prov_ready = 1
unavailable-subtitle: One decision in the states a month.
on-arrival: {!
Q.union_influence += 2;
Q.repression += 1;
window.RF.stateAction(Q, 'prussia', 1.0);
!}

= Prussia

Communist slates contest the council elections in the big works; unemployed committees march on the town halls to demand relief.

- @prussia: Back to Prussia.
- @rf_hand: Back to the party.

@prussia_support
title: Back the Social Democratic government in Prussia against the right.
subtitle: Better relations with the SPD; pleases the Right, angers the Left. Some radical voters are disappointed.
new-page: true
view-if: state_spd_gov = 1 and state_kpd_seats > 0
choose-if: prov_ready = 1
unavailable-subtitle: One decision in the states a month.
on-arrival: {!
Q.spd_relation += 3;
window.RF.lean(Q, {right: 2, left: -2});
window.RF.stateAction(Q, 'prussia', -0.5);
!}

= Prussia

The Communist deputies vote with the Social Democrats against the bourgeois motions. The SPD press grudgingly notes it; the Left calls it parliamentary cretinism.

- @prussia: Back to Prussia.
- @rf_hand: Back to the party.

@prussia_attack
title: Attack the government in Prussia from the left.
subtitle: More standing with radical voters; worse relations with the SPD. Pleases the Left.
new-page: true
view-if: state_kpd_seats > 0
choose-if: prov_ready = 1
unavailable-subtitle: One decision in the states a month.
on-arrival: {!
Q.spd_relation -= 2;
window.RF.lean(Q, {left: 2, right: -1});
window.RF.stateAction(Q, 'prussia', 1.0);
!}

= Prussia

Communist deputies table motions for free school meals, price controls and the disarming of the right-wing leagues, knowing the government will vote them down.

- @prussia: Back to Prussia.
- @rf_hand: Back to the party.

@prussia_ruhr
title: Organise in the occupied Ruhr.
subtitle: The miners are on passive resistance, the French on the pitheads. Raises standing in Prussia and the revolutionary mood; draws repression.
new-page: true
view-if: year = 1923 and month <= 9
choose-if: prov_ready = 1
unavailable-subtitle: One decision in the states a month.
on-arrival: {!
Q.rev_situation += 2;
Q.repression += 2;
Q.nationalism -= 1;
window.RF.stateAction(Q, 'prussia', 1.5);
!}

= Prussia

Party organisers move between the pits and the occupation authorities' checkpoints, preaching a struggle against both the French and the German coal barons.

- @prussia: Back to Prussia.
- @rf_hand: Back to the party.

